What changes (lower-tier only):

    Strategy 1 (ETS replaces LSTM): ETS (Error, Trend, Seasonality) is a classical state-space model that handles the same patterns LSTM learns on 500-row data. For financial time series with <1000 rows, tree/ETS models consistently match or beat neural nets. The M4 competition (Makridakis et al. 2020) showed statistical models beat LSTM on short series. Your own plan doc says fit_autoarima was already replaced by ETS (S17 fix) because it's "10-50x faster with equivalent accuracy."
